{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["(<b>And it shall be, when YHWH brings you.</b> Some of our Rabbis learned from here that firstborn animals born in the wilderness were not consecrated. And the one who says they were consecrated explains this 'bringing' as: if you fulfill it in the wilderness, you will merit to enter the land and fulfill it there.)" "<b>Swore to you.</b> And where did He swear to you? ״וְהֵבֵאתִי אֶתְכֶם אֶל הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר נָשָׂאתִי וְגוֹ׳״ (Exodus 6)." "<b>And give it to you.</b> Let it be in your eyes as though it were given to you that very day, and not like an inheritance from the fathers."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:57.127458561Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}